Rāma asks Lakṣmaṇa to reverse consecration bustle --- Rāma bids spare anxious Kaikēyī distress --- Rāma recalls no offense to mothers or father --- Rāma wishes truth-kept father fearless of otherworld --- Rāma foresees Bharata calm consecration after exile --- Rāma attributes Kaikēyī change to fate alone --- Rāma declares fate irresistible in pleasure and pain --- Rāma forbids blaming younger mother overcome by fate --- Rāma urges Lakṣmaṇa to withdraw rites without grief